## What this is
One paragraph. The user, the job, the non-goals.

## Commands
- `make check` before every commit and before you say you are done.
- `make test`, `make build`, `make run`. Bare `make` lists the targets.

## Workflow
- Issues live in beads. Run `bd prime` at session start. One bead per branch.
- Never work outside the files your bead names. If scope grows, create a new bead.
- Write the acceptance tests first and show them failing.
- Small commits, Conventional Commits format, `Refs: <bead-id>` in the footer.

## Rules
- Every status line reflects the real result. No unconditional success.
- Do not read or write secrets. Use `.env.example` names only.
- Do not add a dependency without saying why in the PR.
- Prefer refactoring to rewriting.
- If the same test fails three times, stop and report. Do not try a fourth patch.

## Go conventions
- `cmd/{{.Name}}/main.go` stays thin; logic lives under `internal/`.
- Tests sit beside the code and are table-driven.
- Wrap errors with `%w`; compare with `errors.Is` and `errors.As`.
- Standard library first.

## Architecture
See docs/architecture.md and docs/adr/. Read the ADRs your bead touches.

